NevB <neville.burnell@gmail.com> wrote:
> Hi,
>
> Is it possible to customise the monster colors used by Nethack - I
> don't notice some of the darker colors from time to time which is a
> cause for frustration.

With this you can change the colors of the windows console:
http://bilious.homelinux.org/~paxed/wintermcolors.php

Vanilla doesn't have the ability to customize the color of monsters.
The only thing you can do is change the used colors with the option
"videocolors".


The next release of UnNetHack will allow you to change the color of
specific monsters in your config file:
MONSTERCOLOR='floating eye':lightmagenta

> Also, boulders show up on my system as an apostrophe, which makes
> sokoban trickier than it needs to be - I'd like to change that too if
> possible.

OPTIONS=boulder:0

